//// damage-behind-a-call-direct-calls/the-callee-puts-a-method-in-front-of-an-inherited-one.ts
// A typed caller reads an object, makes a call and reads it again. The function that it calls gives the class a method of its own under a name that it has inherited so far.
// `strike` multiplies a variable that is declared a number. In the rounds of the damage the variable holds an object, so the multiplication leaves its typed path and runs valueOf, which does the damage.
